{
  "subtype": "focus_inference",
  "implied_focus": "The nature and resolution of the underlying technical failure described in each incident ticket (what broke, why, and what it takes to fix it).",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "incident_category",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Identifies the affected component/system (printer, monitor, network), grounding what kind of thing failed -- a core facet of the failure focus."
    },
    {
      "name": "failure_type",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Directly characterizes the mode of failure (service failure, unresponsive, physical damage), central to the implied focus."
    },
    {
      "name": "resolution_action_type",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Captures what fix is required (repair, replacement, config), a natural downstream facet of failure characterization."
    },
    {
      "name": "self_resolved",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Indicates whether the failure resolved without intervention, a coherent outcome facet tied to failure handling."
    },
    {
      "name": "is_repeat_incident_type",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Flags recurrence of the failure type, an analytically useful attribute of the failure pattern (though the 452/48 skew is suspect)."
    },
    {
      "name": "urgency_signal",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Derived urgency of the failure from the description, a reasonable severity facet, mildly redundant with existing priority."
    }
  ],
  "focus_coherence": 0.88,
  "structure_quality": 0.82,
  "focus_actionability": 0.85,
  "rationale": "The six columns cohere tightly around a single inferable focus: characterizing the technical failure behind each incident and its resolution. They form a sound multi-facet structure -- affected component (incident_category), failure mode (failure_type), required fix (resolution_action_type), and outcome/severity attributes (self_resolved, is_repeat_incident_type, urgency_signal) -- all extractable from short_description rather than restating existing structured fields. This is not a grab-bag nor a single restatement, and the focus is genuinely actionable (an analyst could prioritize fixes, target recurring failure classes, or reduce repair volume). Minor deductions: urgency_signal partially overlaps existing priority, and the extreme skews on is_repeat_incident_type (90% true) and self_resolved suggest weaker/coarser inference on those facets, slightly reducing structure quality."
}

